WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.891
This work makes three contributions.

00:00:03.971 --> 00:00:07.862
First,

00:00:07.942 --> 00:00:11.833
it is the first theoretical characterization of how
to train a Transformer that keeps

00:00:11.913 --> 00:00:15.804
both nonlinear self-attention and a nonlinear MLP,

00:00:15.884 --> 00:00:19.775
and it proves the trained model generalizes in
context to unseen tasks,

00:00:19.855 --> 00:00:23.745
quantifying the required amount of data, number of
iterations, and context length.

00:00:23.825 --> 00:00:27.716
Second, it expands our understanding of the
mechanism of in-context learning,

00:00:27.796 --> 00:00:31.687
showing how the attention layer and the MLP layer
cooperate to make correct predictions.

00:00:31.767 --> 00:00:35.658
Third,

00:00:35.738 --> 00:00:39.629
it provides the first theoretical analysis of
magnitude-based pruning for in-context learning,

00:00:39.709 --> 00:00:43.600
proving that removing low-magnitude neurons is
essentially harmless.
